[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:154] 2026-10-26 14:39:07,531 >> Find the units digit of the sum, $$ 1! + 2! + 3! + \cdots + 2006!. $$<｜Assistant｜><think>
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:154] 2026-10-26 14:39:07,531 >> Okay, so I have this problem where I need to find the units digit of the sum 1! + 2! + 3! + ... + 2006!. Hmm, units digit... that's the last digit of the number when it's written out. So, I need to figure out what the last digit is when you add up all these factorials from 1! to 2006!.
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:154] 2026-10-26 14:39:07,531 >> 
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:154] 2026-10-26 14:39:07,531 >> Let me start by recalling what a factorial is. The factorial of a number n, denoted as n!, is the product of all positive integers from 1 to n. For example, 1! is 1, 2! is 2, 3! is 6, 4! is 24, and so on. Each factorial grows very quickly, but I only care about the units digit of each term because adding them up will affect the sum's units digit.
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:154] 2026-10-26 14:39:07,531 >> 
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:154] 2026-10-26 14:39:07,531 >> Wait, maybe I can find a pattern in the units digits of these factorials. Let me list out some factorials and their units digits:
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:154] 2026-10-26 14:39:07,531 >> 
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:154] 2026-10-26 14:39:07,531 >> 1! = 1 → units digit 1
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:154] 2026-10-26 14:39:07,531 >> 2! = 2 → units digit 2
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:154] 2026-10-26 14:39:07,531 >> 3! = 6 → units digit 6
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:154] 2026-10-26 14:39:07,531 >> 4! = 24 → units digit 4
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:154] 2026-10-26 14:39:07,531 >> 5! = 120 → units digit 0
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:154] 2026-10-26 14:39:07,531 >> 6! = 720 → units digit 0
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:154] 2026-10-26 14:39:07,531 >> 7! = 5040 → units digit 0
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:154] 2026-10-26 14:39:07,531 >> And so on.
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:154] 2026-10-26 14:39:07,531 >> 
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:154] 2026-10-26 14:39:07,531 >> Hmm, I notice that starting from 5!, the units digit becomes 0 because 5! includes both 2 and 5 as factors, which makes it divisible by 10. So, 5! and beyond will all have a units digit of 0. That simplifies things because adding numbers beyond 5! won't change the units digit of the sum. So, I only need to consider the factorials from 1! up to 4! to determine the units digit of the entire sum.
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:154] 2026-10-26 14:39:07,531 >> 
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:154] 2026-10-26 14:39:07,531 >> Let me write down those units digits:
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:154] 2026-10-26 14:39:07,531 >> 
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:154] 2026-10-26 14:39:07,531 >> 1! → 1
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:154] 2026-10-26 14:39:07,531 >> 2! → 2
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:154] 2026-10-26 14:39:07,531 >> 3! → 6
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:154] 2026-10-26 14:39:07,531 >> 4! → 4
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:154] 2026-10-26 14:39:07,531 >> 5! → 0
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:154] 2026-10-26 14:39:07,531 >> 6! → 0
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:154] 2026-10-26 14:39:07,531 >> ...
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:154] 2026-10-26 14:39:07,531 >> 2006! → 0
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:154] 2026-10-26 14:39:07,531 >> 
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:154] 2026-10-26 14:39:07,531 >> So, the sum of the units digits from 1! to 2006! is just the sum of the units digits from 1! to 4!, since all others contribute 0.
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:154] 2026-10-26 14:39:07,531 >> 
[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:154] 2026-10-26 14:39:07,531 >> Wait, is that right? Because each factorial beyond 4! contributes 0 to the units digit, so they don't affect the sum. So, the total units digit of the entire sum is just the sum of the units digits of 1!, 2!, 3!, and 4!.
